1
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:15,340
Vol .com

2
00:00:45,100 --> 00:00:46,218
I'll be right back.

3
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:34,457
Mushroomon and Floramon had become
slaves of the Digimon Emperor,

4
00:01:34,540 --> 00:01:35,775
and they attacked us.

5
00:01:36,060 --> 00:01:38,472
Ninjimon got into a battle with Shurimon.

6
00:01:38,780 --> 00:01:40,417
Gekkomon was there to help us,

7
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:43,794
and we hid in the underground
castle of Shogun Gekkomon.

8
00:01:44,140 --> 00:01:46,737
Ninjimon secretly
slipped in and put a dark

9
00:01:46,820 --> 00:01:49,644
spiral on Shogun Gekkomon
while he was sleeping.

10
00:01:49,800 --> 00:01:51,060
He went berserk!

11
00:01:51,220 --> 00:01:52,780
We couldn't control him,

12
00:01:52,920 --> 00:01:57,337
so we tricked him into destroying the
Dark Tower and then put him back to sleep.

13
00:01:57,420 --> 00:02:01,700
Working together, we removed the
Dark Spiral and returned home.

14
00:02:05,660 --> 00:02:07,836
Submarimon, let's get out of the sea!

15
00:02:33,900 --> 00:02:35,757
Mega Seedramon's still out there.

16
00:02:35,840 --> 00:02:37,360
Why doesn't he attack us?

17
00:02:37,520 --> 00:02:38,737
He doesn't have to,

18
00:02:38,820 --> 00:02:40,737
because he knows it's
only a matter of time

19
00:02:40,820 --> 00:02:43,920
before our air supply
runs out down here. Huh?

20
00:02:49,900 --> 00:02:52,429
I'm afraid of being
down here in the ocean.

21
00:02:52,920 --> 00:02:55,237
I'd give anything to be
out in the fresh air again.

22
00:02:55,320 --> 00:02:57,557
We were all fine a
little while ago when we

23
00:02:57,640 --> 00:03:00,169
were tracking the signal
of a new digi-egg.

24
00:03:00,960 --> 00:03:02,000
Okay, this is it.

25
00:03:02,100 --> 00:03:04,737
This is a strange place
to find a digi-egg, Davis.

26
00:03:04,820 --> 00:03:07,937
I know, but if the digi-vice says
it's under an offshore oil platform,

27
00:03:08,020 --> 00:03:08,850
we might argue.

28
00:03:08,933 --> 00:03:09,997
Where's the digi-egg?

29
00:03:10,080 --> 00:03:12,877
According to the D3, we're
almost right on top of it.

30
00:03:12,960 --> 00:03:14,254
You mean in the water?

31
00:03:14,500 --> 00:03:15,735
Hope it's waterproof.

32
00:03:15,920 --> 00:03:19,797
Well, I'm just wondering if the egg
belongs to TK or perhaps Carter or maybe...

33
00:03:19,880 --> 00:03:20,710
Hey, wait!

34
00:03:20,793 --> 00:03:22,817
Well, I'm gonna go look for that digi-egg.

35
00:03:22,900 --> 00:03:24,097
Last one, there's a rotten digi-egg.

36
00:03:24,180 --> 00:03:26,360
We should be careful. Hey, wait up!

37
00:03:37,540 --> 00:03:39,737
What are you going to do
to those kids, Master?

38
00:03:39,820 --> 00:03:41,177
I don't have time for them.

39
00:03:41,260 --> 00:03:42,897
I'm taking over the world at noon.

40
00:03:42,980 --> 00:03:44,557
And then I have a lunch date.

41
00:03:44,640 --> 00:03:45,677
Make a seed, Ramon.

42
00:03:45,760 --> 00:03:48,878
You have my permission to
do with them what you will.

43
00:04:01,820 --> 00:04:03,180
Lightning javelin!

44
00:04:07,200 --> 00:04:09,906
This isn't really going
to hang up oil prices!

45
00:04:12,720 --> 00:04:16,073
I've heard of earthquakes
before, but never ocean quakes!

46
00:04:26,800 --> 00:04:28,140
The room is flooding!

47
00:04:28,500 --> 00:04:29,735
What are we gonna do?

48
00:04:30,120 --> 00:04:30,950
Davis, look!

49
00:04:31,160 --> 00:04:33,101
I found an emergency shutoff now!

50
00:04:33,240 --> 00:04:36,828
I classify this as an emergency,
so what are you waiting for?

51
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:38,240
Hit the switch!

52
00:04:45,800 --> 00:04:47,565
Great, the water can't get in!

53
00:04:47,940 --> 00:04:49,477
Yeah, but we can't get out!

54
00:04:49,560 --> 00:04:50,820
And even if we could,

55
00:04:50,980 --> 00:04:55,627
then we'd just be bait because Mega
Seedramon's still out there waiting for us!

56
00:05:04,960 --> 00:05:07,431
I've never been so scared in my whole life

57
00:05:07,760 --> 00:05:10,231
We're not gonna make it out alive, are we?

58
00:05:10,580 --> 00:05:11,997
Why are you so upset, Cody?

59
00:05:12,080 --> 00:05:14,817
I've had this nightmare
ever since I was little

60
00:05:14,900 --> 00:05:17,237
The dream was always the
same I was trapped at

61
00:05:17,320 --> 00:05:19,637
the bottom of the ocean
And I couldn't get out Hey,

62
00:05:19,720 --> 00:05:20,957
we'll find a way out of here,

63
00:05:21,040 --> 00:05:24,097
I promise It was just a dream
By the way, how did it end?

64
00:05:24,180 --> 00:05:25,460
I always woke up.

65
00:05:25,580 --> 00:05:27,297
Well, this doesn't look like a dream.

66
00:05:27,380 --> 00:05:28,837
It sure looks real to me.

67
00:05:28,920 --> 00:05:30,096
What the heck is it?

68
00:05:31,380 --> 00:05:34,780
I do believe it says it's an
emergency ejection vehicle.

69
00:05:34,920 --> 00:05:36,217
All right, we're saved.

70
00:05:36,300 --> 00:05:37,857
Look out, sunshine, here we come.

71
00:05:37,940 --> 00:05:40,060
Uh-oh, it only holds one person.

72
00:05:40,680 --> 00:05:43,209
In that case, Cody
should be the one to go.

73
00:05:43,760 --> 00:05:45,100
He's the one, I agree.

74
00:05:45,260 --> 00:05:47,319
I think we all agree, right, Davis?

75
00:05:47,640 --> 00:05:49,160
Well, how about it?

76
00:05:49,840 --> 00:05:50,670
Yeah?

77
00:05:51,040 --> 00:05:53,393
Of course I agree, Cody's the one to go.

78
00:05:54,180 --> 00:05:55,397
Then it's all settled.

79
00:05:55,480 --> 00:05:56,310
Go ahead, Cody.

80
00:05:56,393 --> 00:05:57,223
Climb into the pod.

81
00:05:57,306 --> 00:05:59,317
The reason you want me to
go is because I'm afraid.

82
00:05:59,400 --> 00:06:00,257
Well, I won't go.

83
00:06:00,340 --> 00:06:01,987
I just have to face my fear.

84
00:06:02,080 --> 00:06:03,117
Cody, are you nuts?

85
00:06:03,200 --> 00:06:04,237
You're going to get out of here alive.

86
00:06:04,320 --> 00:06:07,377
If I was given that chance, I'd
be all over it like a cheap suit.

87
00:06:07,460 --> 00:06:08,813
All right, then you go.

88
00:06:09,340 --> 00:06:11,260
I can't go because you're going.

89
00:06:11,580 --> 00:06:12,880
I am not going.

90
00:06:13,140 --> 00:06:15,997
To be honest, I can't tell which
one of them is the youngest.

91
00:06:16,080 --> 00:06:17,433
Relax, I've got a plan.

92
00:06:17,820 --> 00:06:18,997
Here's what we're going to do.

93
00:06:19,080 --> 00:06:21,497
We'll draw straws and
whoever wins gets to go.

94
00:06:21,580 --> 00:06:22,657
That sounds fair to me.

95
00:06:22,740 --> 00:06:23,570
Not me.

96
00:06:23,653 --> 00:06:24,777
I'm not good at drawing.

97
00:06:24,860 --> 00:06:27,820
That seems like a really
good plan, Yoli. I'm in.

98
00:06:28,020 --> 00:06:29,937
How does that sound to you, Cody?

99
00:06:30,020 --> 00:06:31,120
Uh, mm-hmm.

100
00:06:31,760 --> 00:06:33,717
Don't bother making any
straws for me, Yoli.

101
00:06:33,800 --> 00:06:34,741
I'm not thirsty.

102
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:37,737
Actually, to be fair, they
should make straws for all of us.

103
00:06:37,820 --> 00:06:38,650
I agree.

104
00:06:38,960 --> 00:06:40,097
We're all in this together,

105
00:06:40,180 --> 00:06:42,817
so we should all have an equal
chance to make it out of here.

106
00:06:42,900 --> 00:06:43,730
That's right.

107
00:06:43,813 --> 00:06:45,017
One for all and all for me.

108
00:06:45,100 --> 00:06:47,041
I don't think that's how it goes.

109
00:06:47,540 --> 00:06:49,540
One of them has red on the bottom.

110
00:06:49,840 --> 00:06:50,880
Okay. Wait.

111
00:06:51,120 --> 00:06:52,477
Let's let Cody go first.

112
00:06:52,560 --> 00:06:53,500
Uh, but why me?

113
00:06:53,780 --> 00:06:54,960
Just do it, Cody.

114
00:06:55,680 --> 00:06:56,510
Oh, all right.

115
00:06:59,860 --> 00:07:01,037
Cody, you're it.

116
00:07:01,120 --> 00:07:03,617
I can't believe you picked
the straw on the first try.

117
00:07:03,700 --> 00:07:05,057
Talk about beginner's luck.

118
00:07:05,140 --> 00:07:07,280
That was amazing, Cody. So climb in.

119
00:07:09,300 --> 00:07:11,100
Hey, what'd you do that for?

120
00:07:12,820 --> 00:07:14,657
All the straws have red on them.

121
00:07:14,740 --> 00:07:16,997
The first one was so pretty,
I just couldn't stop coloring.

122
00:07:17,080 --> 00:07:17,910
You cheated.

123
00:07:17,993 --> 00:07:19,797
Oh, right, but we had no other choice.

124
00:07:19,880 --> 00:07:20,710
She's right.

125
00:07:20,793 --> 00:07:22,157
You were being so stubborn about it.

126
00:07:22,240 --> 00:07:23,711
I still don't understand.

127
00:07:23,940 --> 00:07:27,257
I guess they set the whole thing up
so Cody would feel like he had to go.

128
00:07:27,340 --> 00:07:30,037
Do you mean that neither of
you two were in on the plan?

129
00:07:30,120 --> 00:07:31,597
You mean everyone knew but us?

130
00:07:31,680 --> 00:07:32,680
Of course we did.

131
00:07:33,900 --> 00:07:34,730
So what?

132
00:07:34,813 --> 00:07:37,860
I'm still not going. Davis? TK? Right.

133
00:07:39,100 --> 00:07:41,100
Hey, let me go. Put me down.

134
00:07:43,200 --> 00:07:46,957
Now, Cody, make sure you keep your arms
and legs inside the ride at all times.

135
00:07:47,040 --> 00:07:49,477
As soon as you get back, find
Joe and tell him what happened.

136
00:07:49,560 --> 00:07:52,537
Ikakumon's the only one who
can get us out of this place.

137
00:07:52,620 --> 00:07:53,561
Good luck, Cody.

138
00:07:54,440 --> 00:07:55,700
Wait a second, guys.

139
00:07:55,900 --> 00:07:57,018
Let me out of here.

140
00:08:00,320 --> 00:08:03,720
Okay, Mega Seedramon's not
watching. Let's do it. Right.

141
00:08:05,260 --> 00:08:06,840
Okay, I can do this.

142
00:08:06,960 --> 00:08:08,780
I just hold perfectly still.

143
00:08:11,680 --> 00:08:12,740
I made it.

144
00:08:13,660 --> 00:08:14,620
Fresh air.

145
00:08:19,800 --> 00:08:20,960
Hi, this is Joe.

146
00:08:21,360 --> 00:08:23,097
Sorry I can't answer my
cell phone right now,

147
00:08:23,180 --> 00:08:26,117
but I had to turn it off so it
wouldn't ring during my biology test.

148
00:08:26,200 --> 00:08:29,037
I'm pretty good at biology, so
I'll turn it back on real soon,

149
00:08:29,120 --> 00:08:31,137
unless the test is on molecular biology.

150
00:08:31,220 --> 00:08:32,117
Oh, I have to go study.

151
00:08:32,200 --> 00:08:33,030
Bye.

152
00:08:33,500 --> 00:08:35,147
I have to find Joe's school.

153
00:08:41,480 --> 00:08:42,880
Oh, Cody, you're home.

154
00:08:43,620 --> 00:08:46,417
I'm glad, because I have some
errands I want you to run for me.

155
00:08:46,500 --> 00:08:48,277
Now, do you want to write it
down, or will you remember?

156
00:08:48,360 --> 00:08:50,540
Well, I can't. I'm kind of busy.

157
00:08:50,760 --> 00:08:51,936
What's so important?

158
00:08:52,100 --> 00:08:52,930
Well, uh...

159
00:08:53,013 --> 00:08:55,317
Come on, Cody, you can tell me what it is.

160
00:08:55,400 --> 00:08:57,080
I'm sorry, but I can't.

161
00:08:57,240 --> 00:08:59,417
You know I don't like you
keeping secrets from me.

162
00:08:59,500 --> 00:09:01,597
You should not keep asking him about it.

163
00:09:01,680 --> 00:09:02,510
Huh?

164
00:09:02,600 --> 00:09:05,737
If he's forced to tell you something,
he might have to tell you a lie,

165
00:09:05,820 --> 00:09:07,677
even though that's not
what he wants to do.

166
00:09:07,760 --> 00:09:09,417
It's better that he say nothing at all,

167
00:09:09,500 --> 00:09:12,265
rather than say something
that isn't the truth.

168
00:09:12,360 --> 00:09:15,301
There's nothing worse than
telling a lie, you see?

169
00:09:15,940 --> 00:09:18,411
Prune juice sure makes you smart, Grandpa.

170
00:09:21,100 --> 00:09:23,500
I'll be back soon Thanks, Grandpa

171
00:09:25,520 --> 00:09:27,697
Do you have to keep banging your head?

172
00:09:27,780 --> 00:09:29,427
You're driving me crazy Huh?

173
00:09:29,820 --> 00:09:34,957
It hurts just watching you I'll
stop when you stop tapping your foot

174
00:09:35,040 --> 00:09:39,420
like that It's rather annoying How
about if I tap my foot on your head?

175
00:09:39,580 --> 00:09:44,820
There's no reason for you two to be fighting
We're not Or arguing We're not Good,

176
00:09:44,980 --> 00:09:46,686
well, I'm glad that's settled

177
00:09:46,780 --> 00:09:47,610
Ah.

178
00:09:47,693 --> 00:09:49,477
Now, how about a nice game of checkers?

179
00:09:49,560 --> 00:09:51,297
We could use my shell as the board.

180
00:09:51,380 --> 00:09:54,597
I'm sorry, but I don't feel
like playing a game right now.

181
00:09:54,680 --> 00:09:56,117
Forgive me, Armadillo Mom,

182
00:09:56,200 --> 00:09:58,797
but how can you be thinking of
playing games at a time like this?

183
00:09:58,880 --> 00:10:01,497
Easy, because I know Cody
will come and rescue us.

184
00:10:01,580 --> 00:10:03,700
We all know Cody will try his best,

185
00:10:03,880 --> 00:10:06,939
but I just don't know if
he'll make it back in time.

186
00:10:07,100 --> 00:10:09,877
My guess is that we've only
got a couple of hours left,

187
00:10:09,960 --> 00:10:13,195
and shortly after that we'll
completely run out of air.

188
00:10:20,340 --> 00:10:24,977
i'm sorry but he's taking a test right
now but this is an emergency i need

189
00:10:25,060 --> 00:10:30,337
to see joe the rules say don't interrupt
anyone during the test now if there

190
00:10:30,420 --> 00:10:33,437
had been some kind of accident or
maybe a member of his family was rushed

191
00:10:33,520 --> 00:10:37,017
to a hospital or something like that it
would be a different story Otherwise,

192
00:10:37,100 --> 00:10:38,100
you have to wait.

193
00:10:38,840 --> 00:10:40,460
But there was an accident.

194
00:10:44,400 --> 00:10:47,047
And someone might have
to go to the hospital.

195
00:10:52,860 --> 00:10:55,507
There's nothing worse
than lying, understand?

196
00:10:56,640 --> 00:10:58,720
Yeah, but what do I do now?

197
00:11:34,300 --> 00:11:36,017
T .K., what are you doing over there?

198
00:11:36,100 --> 00:11:39,757
I think the digi-egg is buried somewhere
in here, so I'm trying to find it.

199
00:11:39,840 --> 00:11:42,517
Shouldn't you be more worried
about trying to get out of here?

200
00:11:42,600 --> 00:11:45,297
I just didn't feel like sitting
around here doing nothing,

201
00:11:45,380 --> 00:11:48,086
so I figured at least
let's find the digi-egg.

202
00:11:49,800 --> 00:11:51,457
That sounds like a good idea.

203
00:11:51,540 --> 00:11:52,760
Let's help. Right.

204
00:11:53,020 --> 00:11:55,900
What do you say, shall we? Sure. Yeah.

205
00:11:56,680 --> 00:11:57,510
Black.

206
00:11:58,580 --> 00:12:00,051
My dad's in the hospital?

207
00:12:00,660 --> 00:12:01,640
Hold on, Pa!

208
00:12:02,640 --> 00:12:06,557
Sorry I lied and said your dad was
sick, But I had to get you out of class.

209
00:12:06,640 --> 00:12:07,757
Don't worry about it, Cody.

210
00:12:07,840 --> 00:12:09,497
I'm just glad to know my dad's okay.

211
00:12:09,580 --> 00:12:12,737
Besides, this is a real emergency
and you had no other choice.

212
00:12:12,820 --> 00:12:15,837
Yeah, but since your dad's all
right, why are you still running?

213
00:12:15,920 --> 00:12:17,080
Oh, right, yeah.

214
00:12:17,400 --> 00:12:19,117
Let's see, I've got to
turn my phone back on.

215
00:12:19,200 --> 00:12:20,030
Now?

216
00:12:20,113 --> 00:12:21,037
We're running out of time.

217
00:12:21,120 --> 00:12:23,237
I realize that, but I've got to tell Izzy.

218
00:12:23,320 --> 00:12:26,897
For once in your life, get off
the computer and answer the phone.

219
00:12:26,980 --> 00:12:28,156
Hey, Izzy, it's Joe.

220
00:12:28,300 --> 00:12:31,457
The others are trapped under an offshore
oil platform and they need our help.

221
00:12:31,540 --> 00:12:35,187
Now I want you to try to track
down a very old friend of ours.

222
00:12:44,820 --> 00:12:46,120
I guess it's not mine.

223
00:12:46,420 --> 00:12:48,597
Then that must mean it belongs to Cody.

224
00:12:48,680 --> 00:12:51,977
Yeah, and that means that I'm the
one who gets to arm a Digivolve.

225
00:12:52,060 --> 00:12:52,890
Yee-haw!

226
00:12:52,973 --> 00:12:55,077
I wonder what kind of
Digimon you're gonna be.

227
00:12:55,160 --> 00:12:58,000
I think I have a pretty
good idea. Like this.

228
00:13:00,820 --> 00:13:02,702
I think it'll be more like this.

229
00:13:03,820 --> 00:13:06,317
Kind of like a porcupine I kind of hope

230
00:13:06,400 --> 00:13:13,060
he's the handsome one I don't get it,

231
00:13:13,180 --> 00:13:14,497
how come everyone's laughing?

232
00:13:14,580 --> 00:13:16,457
It's just one of those times when you feel

233
00:13:16,540 --> 00:13:19,660
like you can't help but
laugh That's right See,

234
00:13:19,940 --> 00:13:21,117
everyone's so tired,

235
00:13:21,200 --> 00:13:25,612
they're pretending nothing's wrong
Laughter's just a way to cover things up

236
00:13:25,880 --> 00:13:29,340
You know, sort of like I
do in the cat box How sad

237
00:13:31,500 --> 00:13:33,317
Yaliya, are you going to be all right?

238
00:13:33,400 --> 00:13:34,230
I think so.

239
00:13:34,480 --> 00:13:35,740
Am I seeing things?

240
00:13:36,940 --> 00:13:37,980
A Gokimon.

241
00:13:40,580 --> 00:13:43,240
Look, everybody, a
Kakumon's here to save us.

242
00:13:43,360 --> 00:13:46,180
A Gokimon.

243
00:13:46,380 --> 00:13:47,360
Sorry I'm late.

244
00:13:52,180 --> 00:13:54,480
It's Mega Seadramon, my old foe.

245
00:13:55,360 --> 00:13:58,837
He's an ultimate level Digimon
who destroys his enemies

246
00:13:58,920 --> 00:14:02,160
with his lightning javelin
and mega ice blast attacks.

247
00:14:02,460 --> 00:14:04,497
I have faced him once before in Tokyo,

248
00:14:04,580 --> 00:14:08,580
but I don't think I could defeat
him unless I Digivolve to Zudomon.

249
00:14:12,120 --> 00:14:12,950
Ikkakumon!

250
00:14:14,580 --> 00:14:15,760
